{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 2 - Training U-Net for Gap-Filling (Generic - Streaming)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Self-supervised streaming training pipeline** for any Level-3 ocean variable.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook trains a U-Net to fill gaps in satellite ocean observations using **xbatcher streaming** to keep memory bounded. Works for:\n",
    "- Chlorophyll-a (PACE, Copernicus, CMEMS)\n",
    "- Sea surface temperature\n",
    "- Any other gridded ocean variable with cloud/missing data\n",
    "\n",
    "## Key Features\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Streaming workflow**: Zarr \u2192 xarray/Dask \u2192 xbatcher \u2192 TensorFlow\n",
    "- **Memory-bounded**: Never loads full dataset into RAM\n",
    "- **Spatial chunking**: 40\u00d756 tiles (or configurable)\n",
    "- **Generic target variable**: Not hardcoded to chlorophyll\n",
    "- **Self-supervised**: No gap-free truth needed  \n",
    "- **Synthetic clouds**: Temporally-correlated fake gaps for training/eval\n",
    "\n",
    "## Workflow\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Zarr (on-disk)\n",
    "  \u2193 xr.open_zarr with chunks\n",
    "Lazy xarray/Dask Dataset\n",
    "  \u2193 build_standardized_lazy (no .load())\n",
    "Lazy standardized channels\n",
    "  \u2193 xbatcher.BatchGenerator\n",
    "Spatial tiles (time \u00d7 40\u00d756)\n",
    "  \u2193 make_tf_gen \u2192 tf.data.Dataset\n",
    "Training batches\n",
    "  \u2193\n",
    "model.fit()\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install mindthegap if needed\n",
    "# %pip install --force-reinstall --no-cache-dir \"git+https://github.com/SAFS-Varanasi-Internship/mindthegap.git@streamlined-pipeline\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "os.environ[\"TF_CPP_MIN_LOG_LEVEL\"] = \"2\"  # Reduce TensorFlow verbosity\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import xarray as xr\n",
    "import tensorflow as tf\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import mindthegap as mtg\n",
    "\n",
    "# Enable GPU memory growth (prevents cuDNN crashes)\n",
    "for gpu in tf.config.list_physical_devices('GPU'):\n",
    "    tf.config.experimental.set_memory_growth(gpu, True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"TensorFlow version: {tf.__version__}\")\n",
    "print(f\"GPUs available: {len(tf.config.list_physical_devices('GPU'))}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load Your Data\n",
    "\n",
    "Load your xarray Dataset with **time, lat, lon** dimensions.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Requirements:\n",
    "- Target variable (e.g., `chlor_a`, `sst`, `analysed_sst`)\n",
    "- Cloud/missing flag variable (1 = cloud/missing, 0 = valid data)\n",
    "- Land flag variable (1 = land, 0 = ocean)\n",
    "- Optional: Additional predictor variables (SST, winds, salinity, etc.)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Data Source Examples:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Example 1: PACE Chlorophyll (AWS us-west-2 required)\n",
    "# Uncomment to use:\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "import earthaccess\n",
    "import icechunk as ic\n",
    "\n",
    "def load_pace_chl(lat_slice, lon_slice):\n",
    "    auth = earthaccess.login()\n",
    "    creds = auth.get_s3_credentials(daac=\"OBDAAC\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    url = \"https://data.source.coop/fish-pace/pace-oci/inregion/PACE_OCI_L3M_CHL\"\n",
    "    storage = ic.http_storage(url)\n",
    "    vc = ic.credentials.containers_credentials({\n",
    "        \"s3://ob-cumulus-prod-public/\": ic.credentials.s3_credentials(\n",
    "            access_key_id=creds[\"accessKeyId\"],\n",
    "            secret_access_key=creds[\"secretAccessKey\"],\n",
    "            session_token=creds[\"sessionToken\"]\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    })\n",
    "    \n",
    "    store = ic.Repository.open(storage, authorize_virtual_chunk_access=vc).readonly_session(\"main\").store\n",
    "    ds = xr.open_zarr(store, consolidated=False, group=\"daily/0p1deg/chunks_512\", chunks={})\n",
    "    ds = ds.sel(lat=lat_slice, lon=lon_slice)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Derive land and cloud flags (PACE doesn't have explicit flags)\n",
    "    gap = ds['chlor_a'].isnull()\n",
    "    land = gap.all(dim='time')\n",
    "    ds['land_flag'] = land.astype('int8')\n",
    "    ds['cloud_flag'] = (gap & ~land).astype('int8')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return ds\n",
    "\n",
    "ds = load_pace_chl(lat_slice=slice(31, 5), lon_slice=slice(42, 80))\n",
    "target_var = 'chlor_a'\n",
    "missing_flag_var = 'cloud_flag'\n",
    "land_flag_var = 'land_flag'\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "pass"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Example 2: Copernicus GlobColour (via icechunk)\n",
    "# Uncomment to use:\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "import icechunk as ic\n",
    "\n",
    "def load_copernicus_chl(lat_slice, lon_slice, time_slice):\n",
    "    url = \"https://data.source.coop/earthmover/noaa-coastwatch-coastwatch-tb-chlor-a\"\n",
    "    storage = ic.http_storage(url)\n",
    "    store = ic.Repository.open(storage).readonly_session(\"main\").store\n",
    "    ds = xr.open_zarr(store, consolidated=False, chunks={})\n",
    "    ds = ds.sel(lat=lat_slice, lon=lon_slice, time=time_slice)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # flags variable: 1=land, 2=cloud_shore, 4=cloud, etc.\n",
    "    ds['land_flag'] = ((ds['flags'] & 1) > 0).astype('int8')\n",
    "    ds['cloud_flag'] = ((ds['flags'] & (2 | 4)) > 0).astype('int8')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return ds\n",
    "\n",
    "ds = load_copernicus_chl(\n",
    "    lat_slice=slice(30, 0), \n",
    "    lon_slice=slice(40, 80),\n",
    "    time_slice=slice('1997-01-01', '2002-12-31')\n",
    ")\n",
    "target_var = 'CHL'\n",
    "missing_flag_var = 'cloud_flag'\n",
    "land_flag_var = 'land_flag'\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "pass"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Example 3: CMEMS (Google Cloud Storage)\n",
    "# Uncomment to use:\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "ds = xr.open_dataset(\n",
    "    \"gcs://nmfs_odp_nwfsc/CB/mind_the_chl_gap/IO.zarr\",\n",
    "    engine=\"zarr\",\n",
    "    backend_kwargs={\"storage_options\": {\"token\": \"anon\"}},\n",
    "    consolidated=True\n",
    ")\n",
    "ds = ds.sel(lat=slice(31, 5), lon=slice(42, 80))\n",
    "\n",
    "target_var = 'CHL_cmes-level3'\n",
    "missing_flag_var = 'CHL_cmes-cloud'\n",
    "land_flag_var = 'CHL_cmes-land'\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "pass"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "# USER CONFIGURATION: Modify this cell for your dataset\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "# Replace with your actual data loading code (use one of the examples above)\n",
    "ds = xr.open_zarr(\"your_data.zarr\")  # REPLACE THIS\n",
    "\n",
    "# Specify your variable names\n",
    "target_var = \"chlor_a\"  # Variable to gap-fill\n",
    "missing_flag_var = \"cloud_flag\"  # 1 = missing/cloud, 0 = valid\n",
    "land_flag_var = \"land_flag\"  # 1 = land, 0 = ocean\n",
    "\n",
    "# Optional: Additional predictor features (empty list if none)\n",
    "feature_vars = []  # e.g., ['sst', 'u_wind', 'v_wind', 'air_temp']\n",
    "\n",
    "# Preprocessing options\n",
    "log_transform = True  # Apply log to target? (True for chlorophyll, False for SST)\n",
    "n_temporal_lags = 1  # Number of prev/next day channels (1 = prev1, next1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Dataset dimensions: {dict(ds.sizes)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Target variable: {target_var}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Date range: {pd.to_datetime(ds.time.values[0])} to {pd.to_datetime(ds.time.values[-1])}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Crop to U-Net-compatible dimensions (multiples of 8)\n",
    "ds = mtg.crop_to_multiple(ds, multiple=8)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nAfter cropping to multiple of 8:\")\n",
    "print(f\"Dimensions: {dict(ds.sizes)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check data quality\n",
    "target_data = ds[target_var].values\n",
    "if log_transform:\n",
    "    target_data = np.log(np.where(target_data > 0, target_data, np.nan))\n",
    "\n",
    "observed_frac = np.mean(np.isfinite(target_data))\n",
    "print(f\"Observed pixels: {observed_frac:.1%}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Missing pixels: {1-observed_frac:.1%}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if observed_frac < 0.05:\n",
    "    print(\"\\n\u26a0\ufe0f  WARNING: Very few observed pixels. Consider:\")\n",
    "    print(\"   - Different time period\")\n",
    "    print(\"   - Larger spatial region\")\n",
    "    print(\"   - Multi-day composites (resample to weekly/monthly)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Build Standardized Channels\n",
    "\n",
    "Use `build_standardized_lazy_new()` to create standardized predictors and synthetic clouds.\n",
    "\n",
    "### What it creates:\n",
    "- `full_target` - log-transformed target (if enabled)\n",
    "- `masked_target` - target with synthetic clouds applied\n",
    "- `masked_target_m{i}`, `masked_target_p{i}` - temporal lags (prev/next days)\n",
    "- `day_sin`, `day_cos` - seasonal encoding\n",
    "- Flags: `land_flag`, `true_missing_flag`, `valid_masked_target_flag`, `synthetic_missing_flag`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define train period (for computing standardization stats)\n",
    "# Use 60% of data for training stats\n",
    "train_start = str(pd.to_datetime(ds.time.values[0]).date())\n",
    "train_years = int(0.6 * len(ds.time.values) / 365)  # Approximate years\n",
    "train_end_date = pd.to_datetime(ds.time.values[0]) + pd.DateOffset(years=max(1, train_years))\n",
    "train_dates = slice(train_start, str(train_end_date.date()))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Training period for stats: {train_dates}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Build standardized dataset\n",
    "ds_std, stats = mtg.build_standardized_lazy_new(\n",
    "    ds,\n",
    "    target_variable=target_var,\n",
    "    missing_flag=missing_flag_var,\n",
    "    land_flag=land_flag_var,\n",
    "    features=feature_vars,\n",
    "    train_dates=train_dates,\n",
    "    std_vars=feature_vars,  # Standardize features (not flags)\n",
    "    log_target=log_transform,\n",
    "    missing_flag_shift=10,  # Shift clouds in time to create synthetic gaps\n",
    "    n_temporal_lags=n_temporal_lags,\n",
    "    output_chunks=None,  # Auto-chunk\n",
    "    add_geo=False  # Set True to add spherical lat/lon features\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nStandardized dataset variables: {list(ds_std.data_vars)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nStatistics computed: {list(stats.keys())}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Extract target stats for later unstandardization\n",
    "y_mean, y_std = stats['CHL']  # Note: stats uses 'CHL' as alias for any target\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTarget mean: {y_mean:.4f}, std: {y_std:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Prepare Training Data\n",
    "\n",
    "Load data into memory and create train/val/test splits."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define input channels (order matters!)\n",
    "# Start with core channels, add your features\n",
    "input_channels = [\n",
    "    'day_sin', 'day_cos',\n",
    "    'masked_target',\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add temporal lags\n",
    "for i in range(1, n_temporal_lags + 1):\n",
    "    input_channels.extend([f'masked_target_m{i}', f'masked_target_p{i}'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add your custom features\n",
    "input_channels.extend(feature_vars)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add flags (for reference/masking)\n",
    "flag_channels = [\n",
    "    'land_flag',\n",
    "    'true_missing_flag',\n",
    "    'valid_masked_target_flag',\n",
    "    'synthetic_missing_flag'\n",
    "]\n",
    "input_channels.extend(flag_channels)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Input channels ({len(input_channels)} total):\")\n",
    "for i, ch in enumerate(input_channels, 1):\n",
    "    print(f\"  {i}. {ch}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load data into memory and stack channels\n",
    "print(\"Loading data into memory...\")\n",
    "ds_std = ds_std.load()  # Materialize all lazy operations\n",
    "\n",
    "# Stack into numpy arrays\n",
    "X = np.stack([ds_std[ch].values for ch in input_channels], axis=-1).astype('float32')\n",
    "y = ds_std['full_target'].values[..., None].astype('float32')  # Target with NaN kept\n",
    "\n",
    "# Extract synthetic cloud mask for evaluation\n",
    "synthetic_mask = ds_std['synthetic_missing_flag'].values\n",
    "\n",
    "T, H, W, C = X.shape\n",
    "print(f\"\\nData loaded:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  X shape: {X.shape} (time, lat, lon, channels)\")\n",
    "print(f\"  y shape: {y.shape} (time, lat, lon, 1)\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Synthetic cloud coverage: {synthetic_mask.mean():.1%}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create train/val/test splits\n",
    "# Use contiguous split with buffers to reduce temporal leakage\n",
    "\n",
    "n_train = int(0.6 * T)\n",
    "n_val = int(0.2 * T)\n",
    "buf = 2  # Buffer days between splits\n",
    "\n",
    "train_mask = np.arange(T) < n_train\n",
    "val_mask = (np.arange(T) >= n_train + buf) & (np.arange(T) < n_train + buf + n_val)\n",
    "test_mask = np.arange(T) >= n_train + buf + n_val + buf\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Data splits:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Train: {train_mask.sum()} days ({train_mask.sum()/T:.1%})\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Val:   {val_mask.sum()} days ({val_mask.sum()/T:.1%})\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Test:  {test_mask.sum()} days ({test_mask.sum()/T:.1%})\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Buffer: {buf} days between each split\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Train U-Net\n",
    "\n",
    "Train with standard MSE loss. NaN targets are replaced with 0 (but won't contribute to loss due to masking during evaluation)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Training configuration\n",
    "BATCH_SIZE = 4\n",
    "EPOCHS = 50\n",
    "PATIENCE = 10\n",
    "\n",
    "# Prepare data (replace NaN with 0 for training)\n",
    "y_train = np.nan_to_num(y[train_mask], nan=0.0)\n",
    "y_val = np.nan_to_num(y[val_mask], nan=0.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create TensorFlow datasets\n",
    "train_ds = tf.data.Dataset.from_tensor_slices((X[train_mask], y_train))\n",
    "train_ds = train_ds.shuffle(512).batch(BATCH_SIZE).prefetch(tf.data.AUTOTUNE)\n",
    "\n",
    "val_ds = tf.data.Dataset.from_tensor_slices((X[val_mask], y_val))\n",
    "val_ds = val_ds.batch(BATCH_SIZE).prefetch(tf.data.AUTOTUNE)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Training samples: {train_mask.sum()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Validation samples: {val_mask.sum()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Build and compile model\n",
    "model = mtg.UNet((None, None, C))\n",
    "\n",
    "model.compile(\n",
    "    optimizer=tf.keras.optimizers.Adam(learning_rate=0.001),\n",
    "    loss='mse',\n",
    "    metrics=['mae']\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Callbacks\n",
    "early_stop = tf.keras.callbacks.EarlyStopping(\n",
    "    monitor='val_loss',\n",
    "    patience=PATIENCE,\n",
    "    restore_best_weights=True,\n",
    "    verbose=1\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Model built. Starting training...\")\n",
    "model.summary()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Train\n",
    "history = model.fit(\n",
    "    train_ds,\n",
    "    validation_data=val_ds,\n",
    "    epochs=EPOCHS,\n",
    "    callbacks=[early_stop],\n",
    "    verbose=2\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot training history\n",
    "fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 4))\n",
    "\n",
    "ax1.plot(history.history['loss'], label='Train')\n",
    "ax1.plot(history.history['val_loss'], label='Val')\n",
    "ax1.set_xlabel('Epoch')\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel('MSE Loss')\n",
    "ax1.set_title('Training Loss')\n",
    "ax1.legend()\n",
    "ax1.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax2.plot(history.history['mae'], label='Train')\n",
    "ax2.plot(history.history['val_mae'], label='Val')\n",
    "ax2.set_xlabel('Epoch')\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel('MAE')\n",
    "ax2.set_title('Training MAE')\n",
    "ax2.legend()\n",
    "ax2.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nBest epoch: {np.argmin(history.history['val_loss']) + 1}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Best val loss: {min(history.history['val_loss']):.6f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Save model and metadata\n",
    "MODEL_DIR = \"models\"\n",
    "os.makedirs(MODEL_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "model_path = os.path.join(MODEL_DIR, \"unet_gapfill.keras\")\n",
    "model.save(model_path)\n",
    "print(f\"Model saved to {model_path}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save metadata\n",
    "import pickle\n",
    "metadata = {\n",
    "    'stats': stats,\n",
    "    'input_channels': input_channels,\n",
    "    'target_variable': target_var,\n",
    "    'y_mean': y_mean,\n",
    "    'y_std': y_std,\n",
    "    'log_transform': log_transform,\n",
    "}\n",
    "with open(model_path.replace('.keras', '_metadata.pkl'), 'wb') as f:\n",
    "    pickle.dump(metadata, f)\n",
    "print(\"Metadata saved\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Evaluate (Self-Supervised)\n",
    "\n",
    "Evaluate on held-out **synthetic clouds** only (pixels we intentionally hid).\n",
    "Compare to **persistence baseline** (yesterday's value)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Predict on test set\n",
    "print(\"Predicting on test set...\")\n",
    "X_test = X[test_mask]\n",
    "predictions_std = model.predict(X_test, batch_size=1, verbose=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Unstandardize predictions\n",
    "predictions = predictions_std[..., 0] * y_std + y_mean\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get ground truth (in original log-scale if log_transform=True)\n",
    "if log_transform:\n",
    "    truth = np.log(np.where(ds[target_var].values[test_mask] > 0, \n",
    "                            ds[target_var].values[test_mask], np.nan))\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    truth = ds[target_var].values[test_mask]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get synthetic cloud mask for test period\n",
    "synth_cloud_test = synthetic_mask[test_mask]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compute metrics only at synthetic clouds (held-out observed pixels)\n",
    "mask_valid = synth_cloud_test & np.isfinite(truth) & np.isfinite(predictions)\n",
    "test_mae = np.mean(np.abs(predictions[mask_valid] - truth[mask_valid]))\n",
    "test_rmse = np.sqrt(np.mean((predictions[mask_valid] - truth[mask_valid])**2))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTest set pixels evaluated: {mask_valid.sum()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"U-Net MAE:  {test_mae:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"U-Net RMSE: {test_rmse:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Persistence baseline (yesterday's value)\n",
    "if log_transform:\n",
    "    all_truth = np.log(np.where(ds[target_var].values > 0, ds[target_var].values, np.nan))\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    all_truth = ds[target_var].values\n",
    "\n",
    "persistence = np.roll(all_truth, 1, axis=0)[test_mask]\n",
    "\n",
    "mask_persist = synth_cloud_test & np.isfinite(truth) & np.isfinite(persistence)\n",
    "persist_mae = np.mean(np.abs(persistence[mask_persist] - truth[mask_persist]))\n",
    "persist_rmse = np.sqrt(np.mean((persistence[mask_persist] - truth[mask_persist])**2))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nPersistence baseline:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  MAE:  {persist_mae:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  RMSE: {persist_rmse:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Summary\n",
    "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(\"SELF-SUPERVISED TEST RESULTS\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(f\"Target variable: {target_var}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Evaluation metric: {'log-space' if log_transform else 'linear'} MAE/RMSE\")\n",
    "print(f\"Evaluated at {mask_valid.sum()} synthetic cloud pixels\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(f\"{'Metric':<15} {'U-Net':>10} {'Persist':>10} {'Improve':>10}\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 60)\n",
    "print(f\"{'MAE':<15} {test_mae:>10.4f} {persist_mae:>10.4f} {(persist_mae-test_mae):>10.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'RMSE':<15} {test_rmse:>10.4f} {persist_rmse:>10.4f} {(persist_rmse-test_rmse):>10.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'% Better':<15} {(1-test_mae/persist_mae)*100:>9.1f}% {(1-test_rmse/persist_rmse)*100:>9.1f}%\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "\n",
    "if test_mae < persist_mae:\n",
    "    print(\"\\n\u2713 SUCCESS: Model beats persistence baseline!\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"\\n\u2717 Model does not beat persistence. Consider:\")\n",
    "    print(\"  - More training epochs or data\")\n",
    "    print(\"  - Additional predictor features (SST, winds, etc.)\")\n",
    "    print(\"  - Different missing_flag_shift value\")\n",
    "    print(\"  - Spatial patching (if memory-limited)\")"
   ]
